      "widgets_values": [
        "Replace the blank gray canvas in <image1> with the following complete character image. Use the other images only as references, not as a collage. Render an opaque image. Photorealistic studio character reference. Exactly one person, plain neutral light gray background, soft even light, realistic skin and fabric. No text, no panels, no props unless part of the outfit. <image2> is the approved full-body character: preserve its identity, hairstyle, body proportions, complete clothing, colors, accessories and shoes. <image3> provides fine facial identity only. <image4> provides garment detail only; ignore the face of its wearer. Keep every garment piece on the same part of the body and do not mirror or duplicate patches. If the approved character wears a beret, keep the same fitted size, crown shape, tilt, side drape and low band position while rotating the head. Keep the front insignia on the front part of the beret. If it wears a structured cap or other non-beret hat, preserve its brim, crown and low fit. Keep the eyes clear in either case. Do not redesign, add accessories, change age or change expression. Front-facing head-and-shoulders close-up of the SAME character, whole head and hair or headwear within frame. Match collar and hairstyle to <image2>. Eyes visible, natural neutral expression. No beautification, no face reshaping. Avoid: multiple people, duplicate person, collage, text, watermark, cropped feet, cropped head, extra limbs, deformed hands, different clothes, different identity, fisheye.",
